<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Appendices</p>
</div>
<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Use of LLMs and other tools</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used Grammarly to facilitate writing and GPT-5, Gemini, and Claude to check for mathematical and notational inconsistencies, as well as facilitate writing code.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Arbitrary sources and targets</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the main text, we described our method in the special case of generating flow paths from a Gaussian <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> to a complex density <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here we show that our framework can be readily extended to model flow paths between two arbitrary densities <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\nu</annotation></semantics></math>.
In addition to the single-cell dataset in Section <a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" title="Inference of single-cell gene expression trajectories. ‣ 4.1 Improved representation of geometric datasets ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, this setup is relevant for many other applications <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu, 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Albergo et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
FM naturally lends to this setting as the conditional paths can be conditioned on both source and target samples <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tong et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
First, to approximate the manifold structure, we compute CDC matrices <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0}),\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0}),\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, for training points <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\sim\mu,x_{1}\sim\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\sim\mu,x_{1}\sim\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, as described in Section <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Estimating the carré du champ ‣ 3 Regularised Flow matching on generalised data manifolds ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.
We incorporate these local tangent spaces in the conditional probability path by using the displacement interpolant between <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(x_{0},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(x_{0},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
We formalise this in the following proposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given that <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}(x|x_{0},x_{1})=\mathcal{N}(x_{0},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}(x|x_{0},x_{1})=\mathcal{N}(x_{0},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}(x|x_{0},x_{1})=\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}(x|x_{0},x_{1})=\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math> are Gaussian, the displacement interpolant between them, <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x|x_{0},x_{1}):=[p_{0},\,p_{1}]_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x|x_{0},x_{1}):=[p_{0},\,p_{1}]_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, is also Gaussian, with mean and covariance given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{t}=(1-t)x_{0}+tx_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{t}=(1-t)x_{0}+tx_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E13Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{t}=\mathbf{A}_{t}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0})\mathbf{A}_{t}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{t}=\mathbf{A}_{t}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0})\mathbf{A}_{t}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{t}=\left(1-t\right)\mathbf{I}+t\mathbf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{t}=\left(1-t\right)\mathbf{I}+t\mathbf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}:=\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0})^{-\frac{1}{2}}\left(\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0})^{\frac{1}{2}}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0})^{\frac{1}{2}}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0})^{-\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}:=\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0})^{-\frac{1}{2}}\left(\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0})^{\frac{1}{2}}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0})^{\frac{1}{2}}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0})^{-\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with the corresponding conditional flow being</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t}(x|x_{1},x_{0})=(1-t)x_{0}+tx_{1}+\mathbf{A}_{t}\left(x-x_{0}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t}(x|x_{1},x_{0})=(1-t)x_{0}+tx_{1}+\mathbf{A}_{t}\left(x-x_{0}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Follows from the optimal transport interpolation of two covariance matrices <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0}),\,\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{0}),\,\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bhatia et al., 2019</a>)</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Carré du champ flow matching generates optimal transport flow paths</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since we aim to improve the approximation of the underlying density as <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(x)\simeq\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathcal{N}(x^{(i)},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x^{(i)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(x)\simeq\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathcal{N}(x^{(i)},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x^{(i)}))</annotation></semantics></math> using the carré du champ tangent space approximations <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x^{(i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x^{(i)})</annotation></semantics></math>, a naïve approach might be to randomly augment each training point <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> by some perturbation from <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x^{(i)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x^{(i)}))</annotation></semantics></math>, take the standard conditional OT paths (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.1 Flow Matching ‣ 2 Background ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), and train against the FM loss (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2.1 Flow Matching ‣ 2 Background ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
However, we show that this approach is equivalent to FM between <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(x^{(i)},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x^{(i)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(x^{(i)},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x^{(i)}))</annotation></semantics></math> with non-optimal transport probability paths.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Training an FM model with source points <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and target points <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathcal{N}(X_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathcal{N}(X_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}\sim\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}\sim\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent, in expectation, to training with the conditional probability path</span></p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{t}(x|x_{1})=\mathcal{N}(tx_{1},\,(1-t)^{2}\mathbf{I}+t^{2}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{t}(x|x_{1})=\mathcal{N}(tx_{1},\,(1-t)^{2}\mathbf{I}+t^{2}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which differs from the optimal probability path obtained via displacement interpolation</span></p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x|x_{1}):=[\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}),\,\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))]_{t}=\mathcal{N}\big(tx_{1},\big[(1-t)\mathbf{I}+t\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})^{1/2}\big]^{2}\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x|x_{1}):=[\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}),\,\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))]_{t}=\mathcal{N}\big(tx_{1},\big[(1-t)\mathbf{I}+t\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})^{1/2}\big]^{2}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">whenever <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first show that training with conditional flow paths leading to a naïvely augmented training set leads to the correct marginal probability paths.
We start by considering the FM loss with augmented data, which results in the loss</span></p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{aug}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0},X_{1},Z}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}((1-t)X_{0}+tZ)-(Z-X_{0})\|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{aug}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0},X_{1},Z}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}((1-t)X_{0}+tZ)-(Z-X_{0})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}\sim p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}\sim p</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}\sim\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}\sim\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
Differentiating with respect to <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{aug}}=\mathbb{E}_{X_{1}}\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0},Z}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}((1-t)X_{0}+tZ)-(Z-X_{0})\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{aug}}=\mathbb{E}_{X_{1}}\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0},Z}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}((1-t)X_{0}+tZ)-(Z-X_{0})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The expectation on the right is just the FM loss (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2.1 Flow Matching ‣ 2 Background ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) for an affine flow <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\psi}_{t}(X|Z)=(1-t)X+tZ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\psi}_{t}(X|Z)=(1-t)X+tZ</annotation></semantics></math> between <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Theorem 2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lipman et al. (2023)</a></cite>, we may marginalise over the conditional flows <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\psi}_{t}(\cdot|Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\psi}_{t}(\cdot|Z)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0},Z}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}((1-t)X_{0}+tZ)-(Z-X_{0})\|^{2}=\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0}}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}(\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}(X_{0}))-\frac{d}{dt}\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}(X_{0})\|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0},Z}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}((1-t)X_{0}+tZ)-(Z-X_{0})\|^{2}=\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0}}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}(\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}(X_{0}))-\frac{d}{dt}\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}(X_{0})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the marginal flow between <math id="A2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math>.
This tells us that we can view data augmentation as a distinct FM problem for each training point <math id="A2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We may then take the expectation over these points to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{aug}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{aug}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{X_{1}}\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0}}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}(\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}(X_{0}))-\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}^{\prime}(X_{0})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{X_{1}}\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0}}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}(\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}(X_{0}))-\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}^{\prime}(X_{0})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0},X_{1}}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}(\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}(X_{0}))-\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}^{\prime}(X_{0})\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0},X_{1}}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}(\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}(X_{0}))-\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}^{\prime}(X_{0})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">If we define conditional flows between <math id="A2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math> by
<math id="A2.p2.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\psi}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1}):=\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\psi}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1}):=\widetilde{\psi}_{t,X_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>
then</span></p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{aug}}=\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0},X_{1}}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}(\widetilde{\psi}_{t}(X_{0}|X_{1}))-\widetilde{\psi}_{t}^{\prime}(X_{0}|X_{1})\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{aug}}=\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{t,X_{0},X_{1}}\|\hat{u}^{\theta}_{t}(\widetilde{\psi}_{t}(X_{0}|X_{1}))-\widetilde{\psi}_{t}^{\prime}(X_{0}|X_{1})\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">which shows that training with <math id="A2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{aug}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>aug</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{aug}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same, in expectation, as training with <math id="A2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2.1 Flow Matching ‣ 2 Background ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) using the conditional flows <math id="A2.p2.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\psi}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\psi}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Although the above shows that naïve data augmentation is equivalent to an FM problem, we now show that the resulting conditional flow paths are different from the CDC-FM paths, and so are suboptimal.
We can derive a closed-form expression for the conditional path
<math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{p}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{p}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})=\mathcal{N}\big(tX_{1},(1-t)^{2}\textbf{I}+t^{2}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})=\mathcal{N}\big(tX_{1},(1-t)^{2}\textbf{I}+t^{2}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">because, if <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X\sim\tilde{p}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\tilde{p}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=ta+(1-t)b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=ta+(1-t)b</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\sim\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\sim\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math> are independently sampled.
but the optimal probability path between <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(x_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1}))</annotation></semantics></math> is given by the displacement interpolant</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=[\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}),\,\mathcal{N}(X_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1}))]_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=[\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}),\,\mathcal{N}(X_{1},\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1}))]_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}\big(tX_{1},\big[(1-t)\mathbf{I}+t\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})^{1/2}\big]^{2}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}\big(tX_{1},\big[(1-t)\mathbf{I}+t\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})^{1/2}\big]^{2}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}\big(tX_{1},(1-t)^{2}\mathbf{I}+t^{2}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})^{1/2}+2t(1-t)\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})^{1/2}\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{N}\big(tX_{1},(1-t)^{2}\mathbf{I}+t^{2}\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})^{1/2}+2t(1-t)\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})^{1/2}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">which differs from <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{p}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{t}(\cdot|X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, whereas the probability paths used in CDC-FM are displacement (optimal transport) interpolants, those in FM with data augmentation are not displacement interpolants, except for when <math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(X_{1})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, where they both collapse to FM.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This means that, unlike the displacement interpolant paths in CDC-FM, data augmentation is not conditionally optimal.
In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lipman et al. (2023)</a></cite>, the authors show that an FM model trained with deterministic displacement interpolant probability paths requires fewer solver steps to compute a solution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Interpretation of CDC-FM as an anisotropic diffusive regularisation</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fundamentally, our framework seeks to identify the Markov process, whose density at <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> matches the data density <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>.
The CDC-FM flow path (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.1 Diffusive regularisation: Carré du champ Flow Matching (CDC-FM) ‣ 3 Regularised Flow matching on generalised data manifolds ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) introduces a data-driven regularity in this Markov process.
In this section, we justify that the CDC-FM flow path is equivalent to adding a space-dependent, anisotropic diffusion term into the marginal probability path (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.1 Flow Matching ‣ 2 Background ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).
This leads to the Fokker–Planck equation</p>
<table id="A3.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial t}p_{t}(x)=(L^{*}p_{t})(x):=-\nabla\cdot(u_{t}(x)\,p_{t}(x))+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{q,r}\partial_{q}\partial_{r}(A_{t}(x)_{qr}\,p_{t}(x))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial t}p_{t}(x)=(L^{*}p_{t})(x):=-\nabla\cdot(u_{t}(x)\,p_{t}(x))+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{q,r}\partial_{q}\partial_{r}(A_{t}(x)_{qr}\,p_{t}(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the adjoint of <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, the infinitesimal generator of the stochastic process, and <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the diffusion tensor, which adapts to the local geometry of data.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the mean and covariance in (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.1 Diffusive regularisation: Carré du champ Flow Matching (CDC-FM) ‣ 3 Regularised Flow matching on generalised data manifolds ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) do not depend on <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, only on the end-point <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We may therefore prove the following result.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> define a Gaussian probability path</span></p>
<table id="A3.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x)=\mathcal{N}(x;\,m_{t},\Sigma_{t}),\qquad m_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\,\Sigma_{t}\in\mathbb{S}_{++}^{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>+</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x)=\mathcal{N}(x;\,m_{t},\Sigma_{t}),\qquad m_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\,\Sigma_{t}\in\mathbb{S}_{++}^{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t},\Sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t},\Sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are differentiable and independent of <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following Fokker-Planck equation</span></p>
<table id="A3.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial t}p_{t}(x)=\nabla\cdot(\dot{m}_{t}\,p_{t}(x))+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{q,r}\partial_{q}\partial_{r}(\dot{\Sigma}_{t,q,r}\,p_{t}(x))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial t}p_{t}(x)=\nabla\cdot(\dot{m}_{t}\,p_{t}(x))+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{q,r}\partial_{q}\partial_{r}(\dot{\Sigma}_{t,q,r}\,p_{t}(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is Gaussian, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{t}(x)=C-\tfrac{1}{2}\log\det\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}-\tfrac{1}{2}(x-m_{t})^{\top}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}(x-m_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{t}(x)=C-\tfrac{1}{2}\log\det\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}-\tfrac{1}{2}(x-m_{t})^{\top}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}(x-m_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiating with respect to <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\log p_{t}=\frac{1}{p_{t}}\frac{\partial}{\partial t}p_{t}=-\tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}_{t})+\dot{m}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{\Sigma}^{-1}_{t}(x-m_{t})+\tfrac{1}{2}(x-m_{t})^{\top}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}_{t}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}(x-m_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\log p_{t}=\frac{1}{p_{t}}\frac{\partial}{\partial t}p_{t}=-\tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}_{t})+\dot{m}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{\Sigma}^{-1}_{t}(x-m_{t})+\tfrac{1}{2}(x-m_{t})^{\top}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}_{t}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}(x-m_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Further, for a Gaussian density <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we may compute the drift term</span></p>
<table id="A3.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\nabla\cdot(\dot{m}_{t}\,p_{t})=\dot{m}^{\top}\mathbf{\Sigma}^{-1}(x-m_{t})p_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\nabla\cdot(\dot{m}_{t}\,p_{t})=\dot{m}^{\top}\mathbf{\Sigma}^{-1}(x-m_{t})p_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Likewise, for the diffusion part</span></p>
<table id="A3.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{q,r}\partial_{q}\partial_{r}(\dot{\Sigma}_{t,qr}\,p_{t})=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{q,r}\dot{\Sigma}\partial_{q}\partial_{r}p_{t}=\tfrac{p_{t}}{2}\left[(x-m_{t})^{\top}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}(x-m_{t})-\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{\Sigma}^{-1}_{t}\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}_{t})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{q,r}\partial_{q}\partial_{r}(\dot{\Sigma}_{t,qr}\,p_{t})=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{q,r}\dot{\Sigma}\partial_{q}\partial_{r}p_{t}=\tfrac{p_{t}}{2}\left[(x-m_{t})^{\top}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}}\mathbf{\Sigma}_{t}^{-1}(x-m_{t})-\mathrm{tr}(\mathbf{\Sigma}^{-1}_{t}\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}_{t})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Adding (<a href="#A3.E27" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Interpretation of CDC-FM as an anisotropic diffusive regularisation ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) and (<a href="#A3.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Interpretation of CDC-FM as an anisotropic diffusive regularisation ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), we obtain the right-hand side of (<a href="#A3.E26" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix C Interpretation of CDC-FM as an anisotropic diffusive regularisation ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>), which is the desired result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Using Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ Appendix C Interpretation of CDC-FM as an anisotropic diffusive regularisation ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we see that the conditional probability path satisfies</p>
<table id="A3.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial t}p_{t}(x|x_{1})=\nabla\cdot(\dot{m}_{t}\,p_{t}(x|x_{1}))+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{q,r}\partial_{q}\partial_{r}(\dot{\Sigma}_{t,q,r}\,p_{t}(x|x_{1}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial t}p_{t}(x|x_{1})=\nabla\cdot(\dot{m}_{t}\,p_{t}(x|x_{1}))+\frac{1}{2}\sum_{q,r}\partial_{q}\partial_{r}(\dot{\Sigma}_{t,q,r}\,p_{t}(x|x_{1})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where, using our CDC-FM flow path in (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.1 Diffusive regularisation: Carré du champ Flow Matching (CDC-FM) ‣ 3 Regularised Flow matching on generalised data manifolds ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="A3.E30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E30X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{m}_{t}(x_{1})=x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>m</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{m}_{t}(x_{1})=x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E30Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}_{t}(x_{1})=\left[(1-t)\mathbf{I}+t\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})^{1/2}\right](\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}^{1/2}-\mathbf{I})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}_{t}(x_{1})=\left[(1-t)\mathbf{I}+t\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}(x_{1})^{1/2}\right](\widehat{\mathbf{\Gamma}}^{1/2}-\mathbf{I}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">We may then marginalise by taking expectations over <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A3.E29" title="In Appendix C Interpretation of CDC-FM as an anisotropic diffusive regularisation ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) to obtain (<a href="#A3.E22" title="In Appendix C Interpretation of CDC-FM as an anisotropic diffusive regularisation ‣ Carré du champ flow matching: better quality-generalisation tradeoff in generative models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) with</p>
<table id="A3.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{t}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\nu}[X_{1}|X_{t}=x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{t}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\nu}[X_{1}|X_{t}=x]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E31Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{t}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\nu}[\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}_{t}(X_{1})|X_{t}=x]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{t}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{\nu}[\dot{\mathbf{\Sigma}}_{t}(X_{1})|X_{t}=x],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">where we used the fact that, by Bayes’ rule, <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int F(x_{1})p_{t}(x|x_{1})p_{1}(x)dx_{1}=p_{t}(x)\mathbb{E}_{\nu}[F(X_{1})|X_{t}=x]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int F(x_{1})p_{t}(x|x_{1})p_{1}(x)dx_{1}=p_{t}(x)\mathbb{E}_{\nu}[F(X_{1})|X_{t}=x]</annotation></semantics></math> for any integrable function <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dirichlet form and carré du champ.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The global smoothness introduced by the diffusive term induced by the flow path is measured by the (weighted) Dirichlet form <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(f,g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(f,g)</annotation></semantics></math>, which monotonically decreases along the evolution <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. For well-behaved test functions <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,g:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,g:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> this reads</p>
<table id="A3.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{E}(f,g):=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Gamma(f,g)(x)\,dx:=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}(L(fg)-fLg-gLf)\,dx=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\nabla f\cdot A_{t}(x)\nabla g\,dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(f,g):=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\Gamma(f,g)(x)\,dx:=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}(L(fg)-fLg-gLf)\,dx=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\nabla f\cdot A_{t}(x)\nabla g\,dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In contrast to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, the integrand <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma(f,g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma(f,g)</annotation></semantics></math>, known as the carré du champ (CDC), measures the local, point-wise smoothness, and encodes the geometry of the underlying manifold <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jones, 2024a</a>)</cite>.
Note, we recover FM in the deterministic limit, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}(x)\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}(x)\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning the associated generator has no intrinsic mechanism to dissipate energy, thus no smoothing.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Taken together, the spatially varying covariances introduce a source of randomness into the sample paths, which can be interpreted as an anisotropic diffusion. The CDC quantifies this diffusion and relates it to the smoothness of the data itself.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Pseudo code</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present pseudo code for CDC-FM in the case of noise to data and compare it to standard FM in the following algorithms.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.tab1" class="ltx_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure ltx_flex_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_figure_panel ltx_float_algorithm ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" style="width:190.8pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Flow Matching</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Samples <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{x^{(i)}\}^{N}_{i=1}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{x^{(i)}\}^{N}_{i=1}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(x)</annotation></semantics></math> parameterized vector field <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\theta}(x,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\theta}(x,t)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
